# ROADMAP — Project Status, Release Pin & Active Sprint Backlog

File: openOODA/ROADMAP.oot
NORTHSTAR is the vision. SHIPPED is what exists. ROADMAP is the active plan.
Rebuilt from NORTHSTAR vs disk (phalanx 2026-08-16). C emit + gcc remains the product path.

## 1. Pin

  Release: v0.203.0-beta. Product libraries: `ooda/std`. GitHub `openOODA/std` archived. Not a volume cert.
  Product tip (ooda): main. Boards tip: main. Libraries: `ooda/std` on product tip.
  Status: compiler/CLI floor shipped (OPEN-1..92 checked). Libraries live in `ooda/std`. Named emit+gcc+run still required.

## 2. Rebuild

  From `ooda/`:
    export PURE_NO_ARC=0
    OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
    OODAC_BIN=./oodac/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
    ./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo
  Official rebuild is `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`. `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` is opt-in only.
  `oodac check scripts/ci_product.oo` typechecks rails. It does not emit, gcc, or run them.
  Named emit+gcc+run proof is `scripts/ci_open_run.oo`.

## 3. Status words

  done — works, proved on disk
  smoke — small check passes
  partial — part works
  residual — wanted in NORTHSTAR, not yet built
  open — active sprint task
  stale — old leftover words; a later proof closed them

## 4. NORTHSTAR vs disk

  Live check: RAM-cold `oodac check oodac/main.oo` about 164s; disk-warm new-process about 0.02s (179 modules). Not under 10s cold.
  Memory: `PURE_NO_ARC=0`. Memory is freed when the last reference drops.
  Native path: no wasmtime, clang, or special env file for C emit + gcc.
  Std: product tree is `ooda/std`. Floor folders first (power law). Domain folders unproved.
  Agent tools (1.1): JSON diagnostics, outline, reflect, fix, patch — done.
  Runtime (1.2): ARC, spawn, arenas, Landlock, rlimit — done. Pause-free GC and undo-RAM stay later.
  Language (2–4): must-use Result/Option, Option/Result exhaust, E_CAP, const header fold — done.
  Caps / SECRET: missing token and `process_exec` sink refuse — done. Full IFC is a moonshot.
  Backends: C emit + `chs_rt` + gcc is the product path. LLVM / WASM / x86 hello locks are product.
  Bit-identical emit-c of hello is product. Raw gcc `cmp` is a compiler leftover.
  Moonshots stay in MOONSHOTS.oot.

